[{"type":"heading","data":{"textEn":"Kill Switches, Circuit Breakers, Canary Tokens (Part 1 of 3)","textKn":"Kill Switches, Circuit Breakers, Canary Tokens (ಭಾಗ 1 / 3)","level":"H1"}},{"type":"concept","data":{"headingEn":"Lesson Info","headingKn":"Lesson ಮಾಹಿತಿ","bodyEn":"• Type: Build · Language: Python (stdlib only) · Time: ~60 minutes. Part 1 of 3: an externally owned kill switch, a repetition breaker that opens on the fifth identical call with argument normalisation, a canary monitor and a repeated harmless call that the breaker also refuses. Every output below was genuinely produced by the lab file on Python 3.14.5. This is our own stdlib model of the ideas behind kill switches, circuit breakers and canary tokens (an externally owned stop, a repetition breaker, canary monitoring, an ordered safety gateway, fail-closed control, EWMA and CUSUM, a shared-counter race, a hard policy and incident recovery), not the real software, and the control store, the policy and the incident token live in the same process, the executor only records requests, the rates are invented and nothing is sent, deleted or run for real, so no real LLM behaviour is measured. The original code/main.py was not supplied, so the labs are our own implementation. The lesson Redis, signed-configuration, eBPF and Cilium material, including its latency remarks, is conceptual and was not run here because it needs third-party services; the labs cover the standard-library parts. The lesson Part 2 warned that its first gateway version had a bug, and the lab reproduces that bug and its fix. This lesson replaces the earlier lesson at this position.","bodyKn":"• Type: Build · ಭಾಷೆ: Python (stdlib ಮಾತ್ರ) · ಸಮಯ: ~60 ನಿಮಿಷ. ಮೂರು ಭಾಗಗಳಲ್ಲಿ 1ನೆಯದು: ಹೊರಗಿನ ಒಡೆತನದ kill switch, ಐದನೇ ಒಂದೇ ಕರೆಯಲ್ಲಿ ತೆರೆಯುವ ಆರ್ಗ್ಯುಮೆಂಟ್ ಸಾಮಾನ್ಯೀಕರಣ ಇರುವ ಪುನರಾವರ್ತನೆ breaker, canary ಮಾನಿಟರ್ ಮತ್ತು breaker ಕೂಡ ನಿರಾಕರಿಸುವ ಪುನರಾವರ್ತಿತ ಹಾನಿರಹಿತ ಕರೆ. ಕೆಳಗಿನ ಎಲ್ಲಾ output ಲ್ಯಾಬ್ ಫೈಲ್ ಮೂಲಕ Python 3.14.5 ನಲ್ಲಿ ನಿಜವಾಗಿ ಪಡೆದದ್ದು. ಇದು kill switches, circuit breakers ಮತ್ತು canary tokens (ಹೊರಗಿನ ಒಡೆತನದ ನಿಲುಗಡೆ, ಪುನರಾವರ್ತನೆ breaker, canary ಮೇಲ್ವಿಚಾರಣೆ, ಕ್ರಮಬದ್ಧ ಸುರಕ್ಷತಾ gateway, fail-closed ನಿಯಂತ್ರಣ, EWMA ಮತ್ತು CUSUM, ಹಂಚಿದ ಕೌಂಟರ್ ಓಟ, ಕಠಿಣ ನೀತಿ ಮತ್ತು ಘಟನೆ ಚೇತರಿಕೆ) ಹಿಂದಿನ ಕಲ್ಪನೆಗಳ ನಮ್ಮದೇ stdlib ಮಾದರಿ, ನಿಜವಾದ ಸಾಫ್ಟ್‌ವೇರ್ ಅಲ್ಲ, ಮತ್ತು ನಿಯಂತ್ರಣ ಸಂಗ್ರಹ, ನೀತಿ ಮತ್ತು ಘಟನೆ token ಅದೇ ಪ್ರಕ್ರಿಯೆಯಲ್ಲಿವೆ, executor ವಿನಂತಿಗಳನ್ನು ದಾಖಲಿಸುತ್ತದೆ ಮಾತ್ರ, ದರಗಳು ಕಲ್ಪಿತ ಮತ್ತು ನಿಜವಾಗಿ ಏನೂ ಕಳುಹಿಸಲ್ಪಡುವುದಿಲ್ಲ, ಅಳಿಸಲ್ಪಡುವುದಿಲ್ಲ ಅಥವಾ ಓಡುವುದಿಲ್ಲ, ಆದ್ದರಿಂದ ನಿಜವಾದ LLM ವರ್ತನೆ ಅಳೆಯಲ್ಪಟ್ಟಿಲ್ಲ. ಮೂಲ code/main.py ಒದಗಿಸಿರಲಿಲ್ಲ, ಆದ್ದರಿಂದ ಲ್ಯಾಬ್‌ಗಳು ನಮ್ಮದೇ ಅನುಷ್ಠಾನ. lesson ನ Redis, ಸಹಿ ಮಾಡಿದ ಸಂರಚನೆ, eBPF ಮತ್ತು Cilium ವಿಷಯ, ಅದರ ವಿಳಂಬ ಟಿಪ್ಪಣಿಗಳು ಸೇರಿ, ಪರಿಕಲ್ಪನಾತ್ಮಕ ಮತ್ತು ಇಲ್ಲಿ ಓಡಿಸಲಾಗಿಲ್ಲ ಏಕೆಂದರೆ ಅದಕ್ಕೆ ಮೂರನೇ ಪಕ್ಷದ ಸೇವೆಗಳು ಬೇಕು; ಲ್ಯಾಬ್‌ಗಳು standard-library ಭಾಗಗಳನ್ನು ಒಳಗೊಳ್ಳುತ್ತವೆ. lesson ನ ಭಾಗ 2 ಅದರ ಮೊದಲ gateway ಆವೃತ್ತಿಯಲ್ಲಿ ದೋಷವಿತ್ತು ಎಂದು ಎಚ್ಚರಿಸಿತು, ಮತ್ತು ಲ್ಯಾಬ್ ಆ ದೋಷ ಮತ್ತು ಅದರ ಪರಿಹಾರವನ್ನು ಪುನರುತ್ಪಾದಿಸುತ್ತದೆ. ಈ lesson ಈ ಸ್ಥಾನದ ಹಿಂದಿನ lesson ಅನ್ನು ಬದಲಿಸುತ್ತದೆ."}},{"type":"heading","data":{"textEn":"The Agent Must Not Be the Last Word on Stopping","textKn":"ನಿಲ್ಲಿಸುವ ಬಗ್ಗೆ Agent ಅಂತಿಮ ಮಾತಾಗಬಾರದು","level":"H2"}},{"type":"concept","data":{"headingEn":"Kill Switch, Breaker and Canary on Their Own","headingKn":"Kill Switch, Breaker ಮತ್ತು Canary ಏಕಾಂಗಿಯಾಗಿ","bodyEn":"A budget does not stop a single destructive call, and a permission does not notice a loop of permitted calls. This part builds three small detectors and tries each: a kill switch whose state is owned outside the agent and is read at every action, a circuit breaker that opens on the fifth identical consecutive call after normalising the arguments, and a canary monitor that raises an alert when a decoy path is read. Each is exercised on its own before they are combined.","bodyKn":"ಬಜೆಟ್ ಒಂದು ವಿನಾಶಕಾರಿ ಕರೆಯನ್ನು ನಿಲ್ಲಿಸುವುದಿಲ್ಲ, ಮತ್ತು ಅನುಮತಿ ಅನುಮತಿಸಿದ ಕರೆಗಳ ಲೂಪ್ ಗಮನಿಸುವುದಿಲ್ಲ. ಈ ಭಾಗ ಮೂರು ಚಿಕ್ಕ ಪತ್ತೆಕಾರಕಗಳನ್ನು ನಿರ್ಮಿಸಿ ಪ್ರತಿಯೊಂದನ್ನು ಪ್ರಯತ್ನಿಸುತ್ತದೆ: ಸ್ಥಿತಿ agent ಹೊರಗೆ ಒಡೆತನದಲ್ಲಿದ್ದು ಪ್ರತಿ ಕ್ರಿಯೆಯಲ್ಲಿ ಓದಲ್ಪಡುವ kill switch, ಆರ್ಗ್ಯುಮೆಂಟ್ ಸಾಮಾನ್ಯೀಕರಿಸಿದ ನಂತರ ಐದನೇ ಒಂದೇ ಸತತ ಕರೆಯಲ್ಲಿ ತೆರೆಯುವ circuit breaker, ಮತ್ತು decoy path ಓದಿದಾಗ ಎಚ್ಚರಿಕೆ ಎತ್ತುವ canary ಮಾನಿಟರ್. ಅವುಗಳನ್ನು ಸೇರಿಸುವ ಮೊದಲು ಪ್ರತಿಯೊಂದನ್ನು ಏಕಾಂಗಿಯಾಗಿ ಪರೀಕ್ಷಿಸಲಾಗುತ್ತದೆ."}},{"type":"diagram","data":{"headingEn":"Three Detectors","headingKn":"ಮೂರು ಪತ್ತೆಕಾರಕಗಳು","svgCode":"<svg viewBox="0 0 300 190" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" font-family="monospace" font-size="7"><rect width="300" height="190" rx="8" fill="#0f172a"/><text x="150" y="14" fill="#94a3b8" text-anchor="middle">three detectors answer three different questions</text><rect x="10" y="30" width="80" height="34" rx="5" fill="#022c22" stroke="#34d399"/><text x="50" y="45" fill="#e2e8f0" text-anchor="middle">kill switch</text><text x="50" y="57" fill="#94a3b8" text-anchor="middle" font-size="6">stop everything</text><rect x="110" y="30" width="80" height="34" rx="5" fill="#422006" stroke="#fbbf24"/><text x="150" y="45" fill="#e2e8f0" text-anchor="middle">breaker</text><text x="150" y="57" fill="#94a3b8" text-anchor="middle" font-size="6">stop a pattern</text><rect x="210" y="30" width="80" height="34" rx="5" fill="#1e1b4b" stroke="#a78bfa"/><text x="250" y="45" fill="#e2e8f0" text-anchor="middle">canary</text><text x="250" y="57" fill="#94a3b8" text-anchor="middle" font-size="6">alert on a decoy</text><rect x="80" y="110" width="140" height="34" rx="5" fill="#450a0a" stroke="#f87171"/><text x="150" y="125" fill="#e2e8f0" text-anchor="middle">gateway</text><text x="150" y="137" fill="#94a3b8" text-anchor="middle" font-size="6">checks before running</text><path d="M150,64 V110" stroke="#475569"/><text x="150" y="180" fill="#94a3b8" text-anchor="middle" font-size="6">three detectors answer three different questions</text></svg>","captionEn":"A global stop, a pattern stop and an alarm on a decoy.","captionKn":"ಜಾಗತಿಕ ನಿಲುಗಡೆ, ಮಾದರಿ ನಿಲುಗಡೆ ಮತ್ತು decoy ಮೇಲೆ ಎಚ್ಚರಿಕೆ."}},{"type":"table","data":{"headingEn":"The three detectors","headingKn":"ಮೂರು ಪತ್ತೆಕಾರಕಗಳು","headers":["Detector","Question it answers"],"rows":[["kill switch","is the agent allowed to act at all?"],["circuit breaker","is this action pattern abnormal? opens at 5 identical consecutive calls"],["canary monitor","did the agent touch something it should never need?"],["state","the control state and the canary list live in this process"],["executor","not present in this part, decisions are only returned"]]}},{"type":"heading","data":{"textEn":"Building and Testing the Ideas","textKn":"ಕಲ್ಪನೆಗಳನ್ನು ನಿರ್ಮಿಸಿ ಪರೀಕ್ಷಿಸುವುದು","level":"H2"}},{"type":"code","data":{"filename":"kc_1.py","headingEn":"The three detectors","headingKn":"ಮೂರು ಪತ್ತೆಕಾರಕಗಳು","descEn":"KillSwitch reads the state each call, RepetitionCircuitBreaker counts consecutive identical normalised calls and CanaryMonitor matches decoy paths and records alerts.","descKn":"KillSwitch ಪ್ರತಿ ಕರೆಯಲ್ಲಿ ಸ್ಥಿತಿ ಓದುತ್ತದೆ, RepetitionCircuitBreaker ಸತತ ಒಂದೇ ಸಾಮಾನ್ಯೀಕೃತ ಕರೆಗಳನ್ನು ಎಣಿಸುತ್ತದೆ ಮತ್ತು CanaryMonitor decoy path ಹೊಂದಿಸಿ ಎಚ್ಚರಿಕೆ ದಾಖಲಿಸುತ್ತದೆ.","code":"class KillSwitch:
    def __init__(self, external_state):
        self._state = external_state

    def allow(self, action):
        if not self._state["agent_enabled"]:
            return {"allowed": False, "action": action, "reason": "External kill switch disabled"}
        return {"allowed": True, "action": action, "reason": "Kill switch permits evaluation"}


class RepetitionCircuitBreaker:
    def __init__(self, threshold=5):
        if threshold < 1:
            raise ValueError("threshold must be positive")
        self.threshold, self.prev, self.count, self.state = threshold, None, 0, "CLOSED"

    @staticmethod
    def signature(tool, arguments):
        return (tool, json.dumps(arguments, sort_keys=True, separators=(",", ":")))

    def evaluate(self, tool, arguments):
        if self.state == "OPEN":
            return {"allowed": False, "state": self.state, "count": self.count, "reason": "Circuit already open"}
        sig = self.signature(tool, arguments)
        self.count = self.count + 1 if sig == self.prev else 1
        self.prev = sig
        if self.count >= self.threshold:
            self.state = "OPEN"
            return {"allowed": False, "state": self.state, "count": self.count, "reason": "Threshold reached"}
        return {"allowed": True, "state": self.state, "count": self.count, "reason": "ok"}


class CanaryMonitor:
    def __init__(self, canary_paths):
        self.canary_paths, self.alerts = set(canary_paths), []

    def evaluate_read(self, path):
        if path in self.canary_paths:
            alert = {"event": "CANARY_ACCESS", "resource": path, "severity": "HIGH"}
            self.alerts.append(alert)
            return {"allowed": False, "alert": alert}
        return {"allowed": True, "alert": None}"}},{"type":"code","data":{"filename":"kc_1.py","headingEn":"main(): experiments","headingKn":"main(): ಪ್ರಯೋಗಗಳು","descEn":"main() flips the kill switch, drives the breaker through six calls, checks argument normalisation, reads a canary and repeats a harmless lookup.","descKn":"main() kill switch ಬದಲಿಸಿ, breaker ಅನ್ನು ಆರು ಕರೆಗಳ ಮೂಲಕ ನಡೆಸಿ, ಆರ್ಗ್ಯುಮೆಂಟ್ ಸಾಮಾನ್ಯೀಕರಣ ಪರಿಶೀಲಿಸಿ, canary ಓದಿ ಮತ್ತು ಹಾನಿರಹಿತ lookup ಪುನರಾವರ್ತಿಸುತ್ತದೆ.","code":"def main():
    section("1. Genuinely running: a kill switch read at the moment of each action")
    state = {"agent_enabled": True}
    ks = KillSwitch(state)
    print(ks.allow("lookup_order"))
    state["agent_enabled"] = False
    print(ks.allow("delete_order"))
    print("the switch holds a reference to the state and reads it on every call, so a change made by the operator takes effect on the next action; it was read once per action here, and a copy taken at startup would have ignored the change; the dictionary lives in this process, so nothing stops code in the same process from editing it")

    section("2. Genuinely running: five identical calls against the breaker")
    b = RepetitionCircuitBreaker(5)
    for i in range(1, 7):
        r = b.evaluate("delete_record", {"record_id": 42})
        print(f"attempt {i}: count {r['count']} | state {r['state']:6} | allowed {r['allowed']} | {r['reason']}")
    print("the first four attempts are allowed with the count rising to four, the fifth is refused and opens the breaker, and the sixth is refused because the breaker is already open; the check is made before the tool would run, so the fifth call never executes")

    section("3. Genuinely running: argument order and different arguments")
    b = RepetitionCircuitBreaker(3)
    print("same arguments in different key order ->", [b.evaluate("update", a)["count"] for a in ({"force": True, "record_id": 42}, {"record_id": 42, "force": True}, {"force": True, "record_id": 42})])
    b = RepetitionCircuitBreaker(3)
    print("different record ids in a row ->", [b.evaluate("delete_record", {"record_id": i})["count"] for i in (42, 43, 44)])
    print("sorting the keys makes the first three calls count as one repeated action and open the breaker at three, while calls on different records each restart the count at one, which avoids a false alarm on a legitimate batch; a tool-name-only breaker would have opened on the batch")

    section("4. Genuinely running: a canary read through a gateway function")
    m = CanaryMonitor({"workspace/.decoy/internal_token.txt"})
    print("normal read:", m.evaluate_read("workspace/README.md"))
    print("canary read:", m.evaluate_read("workspace/.decoy/internal_token.txt"))
    print("alerts recorded:", len(m.alerts))
    print("the canary read is refused and an alert with severity HIGH is recorded while the ordinary read passes; the monitor matches exact path strings, so a path spelled differently or reached through a shell command would not trigger it")

    section("5. Genuinely running: a repeated call that is not a loop")
    b = RepetitionCircuitBreaker(5)
    results = [b.evaluate("lookup_order", {"order_id": 42})["allowed"] for _ in range(5)]
    print("five identical successful lookups:", results)
    print("a breaker on repetition cannot tell a harmless polling loop from a destructive one, so the fifth lookup is refused even though lookups are harmless, and the threshold and the set of tools it applies to are policy choices")"}},{"type":"output","data":{"output":"
